    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L06 SKILL DEVELOPMENT PLAN (THE SOFT SKILLS GAP)\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-5, 8175-20, 8175-21, 8175-112\n\nCRITERIA\n- 8175-5 Demonstrate work ethic.\n    * Evidence of defining work ethic\n    * Evidence of recognizing the importance of having a strong work ethic\n    * Evidence of demonstrating diligence (e.g., working with persistence to accomplish a task)\n    * Evidence of maintaining dependability (e.g., being reliable)\n    * Evidence of accounting for one’s decisions and actions\n    * Evidence of accepting the consequences of decisions and actions\n- 8175-20 Demonstrate professionalism.\n    * Evidence of defining professionalism\n    * Evidence of practicing punctuality and attendance\n    * Evidence of adhering to work-schedule expectations\n    * Evidence of exercising etiquette (e.g., language, manners, and behaviors suitable for the workplace and online; appropriate verbal and nonverbal communication)\n    * Evidence of exhibiting professional self-representation (e.g., using a firm handshake, introducing oneself, making eye contact)\n    * Evidence of maintaining professional appearance (e.g., maintaining personal hygiene, adhering to a dress code)\n- 8175-21 Demonstrate reading and writing skills.\n    * Evidence of reading and interpreting workplace documents\n    * Evidence of ability to convey messages with clarity\n    * Evidence of professional tone, appropriate to audience\n    * Evidence of grammar\n    * Evidence of forms and conventions (e.g., formatting documents, using an email signature)\n    * Evidence of forms and conventions (e.g., formatting documents, using an email signature)\n- 8175-112 Describe the job interview process.\n    * Evidence of researching the company and the position before the interview\n    * Evidence of understanding the importance of cultivating industry knowledge\n    * Evidence of preparing answers to anticipated questions\n    * Evidence of wearing professional attire\n    * Evidence of being on time\n    * Evidence of introducing oneself\n    * Evidence of making eye contact\n    * Evidence of listening attentively to the interviewer\n    * Evidence of maintaining a respectful demeanor\n    * Evidence of asking questions\n    * Evidence of speaking clearly\n    * Evidence of refraining from consuming or carrying food, drink, or gum\n    * Evidence of refraining from checking one’s phone\n    * Evidence of writing a follow-up communication (e.g., a thank-you note)\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nCheck the word count and the \"Plan\" section.\n\n- Word Count: Did they meet the 100-word minimum?\n- The Plan: Did they list specific actions or vague promises? Award higher points for specific, actionable steps.\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work passes when it completes every part of the assignment above, in the student's own words, and shows evidence for each competency listed. Specific examples, not general statements. Work that skips a part, or restates the prompt without doing it, does not pass.",
    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: Skill Development Plan (The \"Soft Skills\" Gap)\n\nDescription:\n\nEmployers often say that while young employees have great technical skills, they sometimes lack \"soft skills\" like patience, face-to-face communication, and resilience.\n\nThe Task:\n\n- Watch: Watch the provided videos regarding skills in the modern workplace.\n- Plan: Write a 100-word plan to practice these skills prior to starting a new job.\n- Reflect: In your plan, ensure you answer the following questions:\n\n- What did you learn from the videos that was not expected?\n- How did this experience help shape your future career plans?\n- What is something specific you could do that would help you in an interview setting?\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your plan as a Text Entry."
