    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L13 CHHS REBRAND PITCH AND FOCUS GROUP PREP\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-1, 8175-50, 8175-103\n\nCRITERIA\n- 8175-1 Demonstrate creativity and innovation.\n    * Evidence of discussing the importance of creativity and innovation in the workplace\n    * Evidence of brainstorming and contributing ideas, strategies, and solutions\n    * Evidence of developing and/or improving products, services, or processes\n    * Evidence of identifying and allocating available resources\n- 8175-50 Develop presentation skills as a form of business communication.\n    * Evidence of eye contact\n    * Evidence of voice tone and projection\n    * Evidence of appropriate appearance\n    * Evidence of the use of vocabulary appropriate to the audience\n    * Evidence of body language\n    * Evidence of use of technology\n    * Evidence of use of visuals\n    * Evidence of engagement of audience\n    * Evidence of adjustments based on audience size\n- 8175-103 Describe the importance of research in developing a marketing plan.\n    * Evidence of Describe the importance of research in developing a marketing plan\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nReview Slide 5 (Focus Group Questions) first. This assesses the new skill (Competency 103). If the student has written open ended, non biased questions intended to gather data, they receive an A.\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work passes when it completes every part of the assignment above, in the student's own words, and shows evidence for each competency listed. Specific examples, not general statements. Work that skips a part, or restates the prompt without doing it, does not pass.",
    "promptText": "Title: Project: CHHS Rebrand (The Pitch and Focus Group Prep)\n\nDescription:\n\nYou have analyzed the brand. Now, you have to sell the new vision. We are going to use this slide deck to conduct Focus Groups with students and staff. Your goal is to turn your written thoughts into visuals that will spark a conversation.\n\nThe Assignment:\n\nCreate a 5 to 7 slide presentation that summarizes your Brand Audit.\n\nSlide Requirements:\n\n- Title and Hook: Your new \"Tagline\" or \"Theme\" for the school.\n- The Target Persona: Visualize the student body with images.\n- The Gap Analysis: Visually contrast the \"Current Reality\" vs. the \"Desired Future.\"\n- The Vision: Show how your vision aligns with modern trends.\n- Focus Group Questions: List 3 specific questions you would ask a student focus group to see if your brand ideas resonate.\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your presentation file."
