    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L28 MARKET RESEARCH (SURVEY DESIGN)\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-2, 8175-17, 8175-103\n\nCRITERIA\n- 8175-2 Demonstrate critical thinking and problem-solving.\n    * Evidence of recognizing and analyzing problems\n    * Evidence of evaluating potential solutions and resources\n    * Evidence of using a logical approach to make decisions and solve problems\n    * Evidence of implementing effective courses of action\n- 8175-17 Maintain working knowledge of current information-technology (IT) systems.\n    * Evidence of hardware and devices (e.g., peripherals)\n    * Evidence of software and applications\n    * Evidence of cloud-based services\n    * Evidence of file-sharing techniques\n    * Evidence of emerging technologies\n    * Evidence of troubleshooting protocols and techniques\n- 8175-103 Describe the importance of research in developing a marketing plan.\n    * Evidence of Describe the importance of research in developing a marketing plan\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nCheck for the question types immediately.\n\n- Quantitative (2): Are there multiple choice or scale questions?\n- Qualitative (1): Is there an open-ended text box question?\n- Bias Check: Read one question aloud. If it leads the witness, deduct points.\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work passes when it completes every part of the assignment above, in the student's own words, and shows evidence for each competency listed. Specific examples, not general statements. Work that skips a part, or restates the prompt without doing it, does not pass.",
    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: Designing Unbiased Surveys (Google Forms)\n\nDescription:\n\nWe are in the process of designing a new service. To do this successfully, we need to know what the customer wants. However, asking the wrong questions leads to wrong answers.\n\nThe Task:\n\n- Create: Open Google Forms and start a new blank form.\n- Design Questions: Create three survey questions.\n\n- Requirement A: Include two quantitative questions (Multiple Choice or Scale).\n- Requirement B: Include one qualitative question (Open-ended paragraph).\n\n- Bias Check: Review your questions. Do they suggest the \"correct\" answer? If so, rewrite them to be neutral.\n\nSubmission:\n\nClick the \"Send\" button on your form, copy the link, and paste the URL as your submission."
