    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L29 SURVEY REFLECTION\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-10, 8175-103, 8175-105\n\nCRITERIA\n- 8175-10 Collaborate with team members.\n    * Evidence of defining collaboration and teamwork\n    * Evidence of discussing the benefits of teamwork\n    * Evidence of establishing expectations, roles, and goals\n    * Evidence of contributing to the success of the team by sharing responsibility\n    * Evidence of respecting the thoughts, opinions, and contributions of other team members\n- 8175-103 Describe the importance of research in developing a marketing plan.\n    * Evidence of Describe the importance of research in developing a marketing plan\n- 8175-105 Identify the components of a SWOT analysis.\n    * Evidence of strengths\n    * Evidence of weaknesses\n    * Evidence of opportunities\n    * Evidence of threats\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nFocus on the Specific Changes section. Award points only for actionable advice (e.g., \"Change Question 4 to multiple choice\").\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work passes when it completes every part of the assignment above, in the student's own words, and shows evidence for each competency listed. Specific examples, not general statements. Work that skips a part, or restates the prompt without doing it, does not pass.",
    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: Survey Quality Control (The Audit)\n\nDescription:\n\nWe have compiled all of your individual questions into a single Google Form. We need to ensure the flow is logical, the tone is consistent, and the bias is removed.\n\nThe Task:\n\n- Access: Click the link provided to view the current \"Draft Version\" of the class survey.\n- Reflect: Read through the questions as if you were a customer taking the survey.\n- Critique: Submit a response addressing the following:\n\n- Strengths: What works well?\n- Weaknesses: Identify questions that are confusing or biased.\n- The Fix: Give specific changes that should be made.\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your reflection as a Text Entry."
