    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L31 SURVEY ANALYSIS (DATA INTO ACTION)\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-2, 8175-19, 8175-103\n\nCRITERIA\n- 8175-2 Demonstrate critical thinking and problem-solving.\n    * Evidence of recognizing and analyzing problems\n    * Evidence of evaluating potential solutions and resources\n    * Evidence of using a logical approach to make decisions and solve problems\n    * Evidence of implementing effective courses of action\n- 8175-19 Apply mathematical skills to job-specific tasks.\n    * Evidence of performing calculations (e.g., percentages, fractions, addition, subtraction, averages, measurement, conversions, monetary transactions)\n    * Evidence of applying mathematical processes to accomplish job-specific tasks (e.g., estimating required supplies, completing expense reports)\n    * Evidence of managing personal finance (e.g., understanding wage rates, paycheck deductions, taxes, sales receipts)\n- 8175-103 Describe the importance of research in developing a marketing plan.\n    * Evidence of Describe the importance of research in developing a marketing plan\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nFocus on the Citation aspect. Did they connect the suggestion to the data? Award full points only if the data *justifies* the decision.\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work passes when it completes every part of the assignment above, in the student's own words, and shows evidence for each competency listed. Specific examples, not general statements. Work that skips a part, or restates the prompt without doing it, does not pass.",
    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: Survey Analysis (Data Driven Decisions)\n\nDescription:\n\nCollecting data is useless unless you use it to make improvements. Today, you will review the results of our class survey and act as a consultant to improve the operation of our league/event.\n\nThe Task:\n\nReview the Google Forms summary charts and responses. Then, write a response addressing the following:\n\n1. The Data (3 Points of Interest)\n\n- Using 100 words (minimum), describe three specific data points from the survey that you find interesting or surprising.\n\n2. The Suggestion (Action Plan)\n\n- Give one concrete suggestion for how our league/event should be organized or operated differently based on this feedback.\n\n3. The Justification (Cite Your Sources)\n\n- You must cite the survey data to justify your suggestion.\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your analysis as a Text Entry."
